      'b60d3b75-d5e9-4273-a10f-3cfd02631b6f',
      '4738f44c-4994-42b1-aa17-ba2f06af70e0',
      'How much does an interior design project cost?',
      'Every project is different. Costs depend on scope, scale, complexity, location, and the combination of services required. Following an initial conversation, TwentyOne06 provides a tailored proposal aligned with your project''s objectives and budget. We are transparent about fees from the first discussion. No vague estimates, no surprises.',
      '<p>Every project is different. Costs depend on scope, scale, complexity, location, and the combination of services required. Following an initial conversation, TwentyOne06 provides a tailored proposal aligned with your project''s objectives and budget. We are transparent about fees from the first discussion. No vague estimates, no surprises.</p>',
      NULL,
      NULL,
      0, true
    );
INSERT INTO public.faq_entries (
      id, topic_id, question, answer, answer_html, link_label, link_to, sort_order, published
    ) VALUES (
      'e834bbbd-44cb-4da9-aaaa-22a904d27dcf',
      '4738f44c-4994-42b1-aa17-ba2f06af70e0',
      'How do you design spaces that improve customer experience and commercial performance?',
      'We combine design strategy, operational thinking, and a deep understanding of how guests interact with spaces. Every design decision from circulation and spatial flow to material selection and lighting, is considered in terms of how it shapes the guest experience and supports the commercial objectives of the space. This is what we mean when we say we design spaces that perform.',
      '<p>We combine design strategy, operational thinking, and a deep understanding of how guests interact with spaces. Every design decision from circulation and spatial flow to material selection and lighting, is considered in terms of how it shapes the guest experience and supports the commercial objectives of the space. This is what we mean when we say we design spaces that perform.</p>',
      NULL,
      NULL,
      1, true
    );
INSERT INTO public.faq_entries (
      id, topic_id, question, answer, answer_html, link_label, link_to, sort_order, published
    ) VALUES (
      '18d3b67c-dd87-4b96-a5a9-226652c9fab9',
      '4738f44c-4994-42b1-aa17-ba2f06af70e0',
      'How do I start a project with TwentyOne06?',
      'The best first step is a conversation. Share a brief outline of your project - the space, the sector, what you are trying to achieve, and any timeline - and we will come back to you. You can reach us through the Let''s Talk form on our website, by emailing info@twentyone06.com, or by calling us directly. We work with clients across Dubai, the UAE, Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, and the wider GCC.',
      '<p>The best first step is a conversation. Share a brief outline of your project - the space, the sector, what you are trying to achieve, and any timeline - and we will come back to you. You can reach us through the Let''s Talk form on our website, by emailing info@twentyone06.com, or by calling us directly. We work with clients across Dubai, the UAE, Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, and the wider GCC.</p>',
      NULL,
      NULL,
      2, true
    );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    'd950de40-b903-4cda-a752-142ff0cfdf99', 'retail-design-to-young-talent-twentyone06-celebrates-double-victory-at-cid-awards-mena-2025', 'Retail Design to Young Talent: TwentyOne06 Celebrates Double Victory at CID Awards MENA 2025', 'TwentyOne06 is proud to announce two major wins at the 19th annual Commercial Interior Design (CID) Awards 2025 - MENA, one of the region’s most prestigious interior design award ceremonies.',
    '1 Oct 2025', 'Awards', '/journal/retail-design-to-young-talent-twentyone06-celebrates-double-.png', '["TwentyOne06 is proud to announce two major wins at the 19th annual Commercial Interior Design (CID) Awards 2025 - MENA , one of the region’s most prestigious interior design award ceremonies. This milestone recognition cements our position as a leading hospitality and lifestyle design studio in Dubai and highlights the strength of our creative team.","The awards ceremony, held under the theme Cyber Garden , brought together the most influential names in interior design, architecture, and fit-out across the Middle East . TwentyOne06 celebrated in style, debuting our new brand identity and walking away with two awards that reflect both our design innovation and the people who power it.","Award Highlights:","WINNER: - Interior Design Concept of the Year: Retail","Cheese Board UAE, Bluewaters Island, Dubai","Located on Bluewaters Island, Cheese Board’s first flagship outside the Grandiose supermarket network redefines what retail can be. Far from a grocery store with theatrics, the 1,126 sq ft space is a stage where cheese takes the spotlight, design is the stagecraft, and guests become the audience . Commissioned by Grandiose and reimagined by TwentyOne06, the project demanded more than identity work - it called for a complete repositioning of retail into cultural experience . The outcome is a premium yet approachable “ Gallery of Taste ” that celebrates cheese as both a product and a cultural artifact.","Key Design Strategies:","1) Storytelling-driven retail: Displays are organised by narrative, profile, and pairing rather than origin - transforming shopping into discovery.","2) Immersive zones: From tasting counters and curated pairings to The Vault, which elevates rare cheeses on sculptural plinths, each zone is designed to extend dwell time and encourage exploration.","3) Materiality as metaphor: Raw stone, warm wood, and sculptural lighting abstract the textures, colors, and stringiness of cheese, creating a space that feels edible yet refined.","4 )Commercial choreography: Spatial sequencing and merchandising strategy increase premium sales, repeat visits, and loyalty through personalised curation and tasting experiences.","This award win underlines TwentyOne06’s expertise in hospitality-led retail design - proving that with the right mix of brand storytelling, material innovation, and behavioral strategy , even a supermarket-born concept can evolve into a cosmopolitan destination for Dubai’s most discerning guests .","Read more - How we designed Cheese Board UAE","WINNER: Unsung Hero of the Year","Hanaa Azmi","At the 2025 CID Awards MENA, Hanaa Azmi , Design Storyteller and Marketing & PR Manager at TwentyOne06, was named Unsung Hero of the Year . With a background in Fine Art and a Fashion Design degree , Hanaa brings a unique creative lens to interior design communication - blending artistry, narrative, and strategy. he was also featured in Commercial Interior Design’s March issue as one of the Top 16 Creative Women in the Middle East You Need to Know , cementing her influence as a young creative leader.","In just two years, she has transformed TwentyOne06 from a boutique studio into one of the most visible names in hospitality and lifestyle design market, securing over 100 press features, 60+ award entries, and doubling the studio’s digital reach. Beyond just marketing and being mentored by award-winning designer , Govind Shepley, she directs shoots, curates stories, mentors students, and shapes the studio’s voice. Hanaa’s recognition is not only a celebration of her impact, but a reminder that design storytelling is as vital as design itself.","A Milestone for TwentyOne06","Winning two CID Awards in one night marks a pivotal moment in our journey as a studio. Since our founding in 2018, TwentyOne06 has grown from a boutique team into an award-winning global design practice , known for our expertise in hospitality design, F&B concepts, and lifestyle retail spaces .","These awards prove what drives us forward:","Click here to find out the full list of winners at the CID Awards 2025- MENA"]'::jsonb, '<p>TwentyOne06 is proud to announce two major wins at the 19th annual Commercial Interior Design (CID) Awards 2025 - MENA , one of the region’s most prestigious interior design award ceremonies. This milestone recognition cements our position as a leading hospitality and lifestyle design studio in Dubai and highlights the strength of our creative team.</p><p>The awards ceremony, held under the theme Cyber Garden , brought together the most influential names in interior design, architecture, and fit-out across the Middle East . TwentyOne06 celebrated in style, debuting our new brand identity and walking away with two awards that reflect both our design innovation and the people who power it.</p><p>Award Highlights:</p><p>WINNER: - Interior Design Concept of the Year: Retail</p><p>Cheese Board UAE, Bluewaters Island, Dubai</p><p>Located on Bluewaters Island, Cheese Board’s first flagship outside the Grandiose supermarket network redefines what retail can be. Far from a grocery store with theatrics, the 1,126 sq ft space is a stage where cheese takes the spotlight, design is the stagecraft, and guests become the audience . Commissioned by Grandiose and reimagined by TwentyOne06, the project demanded more than identity work - it called for a complete repositioning of retail into cultural experience . The outcome is a premium yet approachable “ Gallery of Taste ” that celebrates cheese as both a product and a cultural artifact.</p><p>Key Design Strategies:</p><p>1) Storytelling-driven retail: Displays are organised by narrative, profile, and pairing rather than origin - transforming shopping into discovery.</p><p>2) Immersive zones: From tasting counters and curated pairings to The Vault, which elevates rare cheeses on sculptural plinths, each zone is designed to extend dwell time and encourage exploration.</p><p>3) Materiality as metaphor: Raw stone, warm wood, and sculptural lighting abstract the textures, colors, and stringiness of cheese, creating a space that feels edible yet refined.</p><p>4 )Commercial choreography: Spatial sequencing and merchandising strategy increase premium sales, repeat visits, and loyalty through personalised curation and tasting experiences.</p><p>This award win underlines TwentyOne06’s expertise in hospitality-led retail design - proving that with the right mix of brand storytelling, material innovation, and behavioral strategy , even a supermarket-born concept can evolve into a cosmopolitan destination for Dubai’s most discerning guests .</p><p>Read more - How we designed Cheese Board UAE</p><p>WINNER: Unsung Hero of the Year</p><p>Hanaa Azmi</p><p>At the 2025 CID Awards MENA, Hanaa Azmi , Design Storyteller and Marketing &amp; PR Manager at TwentyOne06, was named Unsung Hero of the Year . With a background in Fine Art and a Fashion Design degree , Hanaa brings a unique creative lens to interior design communication - blending artistry, narrative, and strategy. he was also featured in Commercial Interior Design’s March issue as one of the Top 16 Creative Women in the Middle East You Need to Know , cementing her influence as a young creative leader.</p><p>In just two years, she has transformed TwentyOne06 from a boutique studio into one of the most visible names in hospitality and lifestyle design market, securing over 100 press features, 60+ award entries, and doubling the studio’s digital reach. Beyond just marketing and being mentored by award-winning designer , Govind Shepley, she directs shoots, curates stories, mentors students, and shapes the studio’s voice. Hanaa’s recognition is not only a celebration of her impact, but a reminder that design storytelling is as vital as design itself.</p><p>A Milestone for TwentyOne06</p><p>Winning two CID Awards in one night marks a pivotal moment in our journey as a studio. Since our founding in 2018, TwentyOne06 has grown from a boutique team into an award-winning global design practice , known for our expertise in hospitality design, F&amp;B concepts, and lifestyle retail spaces .</p><p>These awards prove what drives us forward:</p><p>Click here to find out the full list of winners at the CID Awards 2025- MENA</p>',
    true, 0, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    '7748cf10-690d-4513-af1c-cae7cc3fa3c0', 'twentyone06-nominated-among-top-10-fb-hospitality-design-studios-pro-chef-hospitality-awards-2025', 'TwentyOne06 Nominated Among Top 10 F&B & Hospitality Design Studios - Pro Chef & Hospitality Awards 2025', 'We’re thrilled to announce that TwentyOne06 has been recognized as one of the Top 10 F&B and Hospitality Design Studios for the Pro Chef & Hospitality Awards 2025! This nomination',
    '10 Sep 2025', 'Awards', '/journal/twentyone06-nominated-among-top-10-fb-hospitality-design-stu.png', '["We’re thrilled to announce that TwentyOne06 has been recognized as one of the Top 10 F&B and Hospitality Design Studios for the Pro Chef & Hospitality Awards 2025!","This nomination celebrates our dedication to innovative hospitality and F&B design, where every space we create tells a story, elevates the guest experience, and pushes the boundaries of design. By combining strategy, branding, interior architecture, and storytelling, we craft spaces that are not only visually striking but operationally seamless and culturally resonant.","Over the years, we’ve had the privilege of designing some of the region’s most exciting hospitality concepts, including Nama Yoso, Pitfire Pizza, Flaky Pastry, and VOCO Hotel. Each project reflects our commitment to immersive experiences, curated atmospheres, and a balance of functionality and artistry.","This recognition is a testament to our approach - blending creativity with research-driven insights to help brands stand out, connect with their guests, and deliver memorable experiences.","Help us win!","Cast your vote and support TwentyOne06 as we continue to shape the future of F&B and hospitality design.","[Vote for TwentyOne06]"]'::jsonb, '<p>We’re thrilled to announce that TwentyOne06 has been recognized as one of the Top 10 F&amp;B and Hospitality Design Studios for the Pro Chef &amp; Hospitality Awards 2025!</p><p>This nomination celebrates our dedication to innovative hospitality and F&amp;B design, where every space we create tells a story, elevates the guest experience, and pushes the boundaries of design. By combining strategy, branding, interior architecture, and storytelling, we craft spaces that are not only visually striking but operationally seamless and culturally resonant.</p><p>Over the years, we’ve had the privilege of designing some of the region’s most exciting hospitality concepts, including Nama Yoso, Pitfire Pizza, Flaky Pastry, and VOCO Hotel. Each project reflects our commitment to immersive experiences, curated atmospheres, and a balance of functionality and artistry.</p><p>This recognition is a testament to our approach - blending creativity with research-driven insights to help brands stand out, connect with their guests, and deliver memorable experiences.</p><p>Help us win!</p><p>Cast your vote and support TwentyOne06 as we continue to shape the future of F&amp;B and hospitality design.</p><p>[Vote for TwentyOne06]</p>',
    false, 1, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    '9a6ce96d-8245-4a44-a7b2-2cda3fdcd005', 'dental-nation-by-twentyone06-shortlisted-for-interior-design-of-the-year-health-wellness-at-cid-awards-2025-mena', 'Dental Nation by TwentyOne06 Shortlisted for Interior Design of the Year: Health & Wellness at CID Awards 2025: MENA', 'TwentyOne06 has been shortlisted for the Interior Design of the Year: Health & Wellness category at the Commercial Interior Design Awards 2025: MENA for its project, Dental Nation. This recognition',
    '20 Aug 2025', 'Awards', '/journal/dental-nation-by-twentyone06-shortlisted-for-interior-design.png', '["TwentyOne06 has been shortlisted for the Interior Design of the Year: Health & Wellness category at the Commercial Interior Design Awards 2025: MENA for its project, Dental Nation.","This recognition reinforces our reputation as one of the region’s leading studios for designing healthcare environments that feel elevated, human, and deeply connected to brand identity.","Designing Healthcare Like Hospitality in Dubai","At TwentyOne06, we believe healthcare spaces don’t have to feel clinical. They can feel warm, calming, and even luxurious. Dental Nation is a clear example of this approach. What was once a typical multi-specialty polyclinic has been reimagined as a luxury dental wellness brand, a boutique environment where patients feel cared for the moment they step inside.","Our design philosophy draws on the principles of hospitality design: comfort, ambience, emotional connection, and applies them to healthcare. From the reception to the treatment rooms, every detail at Dental Nation was crafted to reduce anxiety, inspire trust, and elevate the patient journey.","The Power of Brand-Led Design in Medical Interiors","Healthcare interiors often overlook brand storytelling. At TwentyOne06, we see brand as the anchor of every project. Dental Nation embodies this through “Quiet Luxury”, a design language of muted tones, refined finishes, and sensory clarity that aligns with the clinic’s vision of premium, wellness-driven care. The result is not just a dental practice but a physical brand experience.","Setting a Benchmark in Health & Wellness Design in Dubai","From boutique waiting areas designed like lounges, to spa-like treatment rooms and VIP suites, the project blurs the line between clinic and hospitality destination. These design choices not only improve patient wellbeing but also support the clinic’s positioning as a high-end healthcare brand.","Why This Recognition Matters","Being shortlisted for the CID Awards 2025 in the Health & Wellness category highlights our studio’s growing influence in medical and wellness design across the MENA region. It’s proof that our approach, merging functionality with atmosphere, and brand storytelling with operational efficiency, delivers spaces that stand out in a competitive market.","The TwentyOne06 Specialty: Elevated, Branded Interiors in the UAE","Dental Nation is just one example of how TwentyOne06 is redefining healthcare interiors. From dental practices to wellness clinics, our strength lies in creating spaces that feel less like institutions and more like experiences. By fusing brand, hospitality, and functionality, we design environments that patients trust, remember, and return to."]'::jsonb, '<p>TwentyOne06 has been shortlisted for the Interior Design of the Year: Health &amp; Wellness category at the Commercial Interior Design Awards 2025: MENA for its project, Dental Nation.</p><p>This recognition reinforces our reputation as one of the region’s leading studios for designing healthcare environments that feel elevated, human, and deeply connected to brand identity.</p><p>Designing Healthcare Like Hospitality in Dubai</p><p>At TwentyOne06, we believe healthcare spaces don’t have to feel clinical. They can feel warm, calming, and even luxurious. Dental Nation is a clear example of this approach. What was once a typical multi-specialty polyclinic has been reimagined as a luxury dental wellness brand, a boutique environment where patients feel cared for the moment they step inside.</p><p>Our design philosophy draws on the principles of hospitality design: comfort, ambience, emotional connection, and applies them to healthcare. From the reception to the treatment rooms, every detail at Dental Nation was crafted to reduce anxiety, inspire trust, and elevate the patient journey.</p><p>The Power of Brand-Led Design in Medical Interiors</p><p>Healthcare interiors often overlook brand storytelling. At TwentyOne06, we see brand as the anchor of every project. Dental Nation embodies this through “Quiet Luxury”, a design language of muted tones, refined finishes, and sensory clarity that aligns with the clinic’s vision of premium, wellness-driven care. The result is not just a dental practice but a physical brand experience.</p><p>Setting a Benchmark in Health &amp; Wellness Design in Dubai</p><p>From boutique waiting areas designed like lounges, to spa-like treatment rooms and VIP suites, the project blurs the line between clinic and hospitality destination. These design choices not only improve patient wellbeing but also support the clinic’s positioning as a high-end healthcare brand.</p><p>Why This Recognition Matters</p><p>Being shortlisted for the CID Awards 2025 in the Health &amp; Wellness category highlights our studio’s growing influence in medical and wellness design across the MENA region. It’s proof that our approach, merging functionality with atmosphere, and brand storytelling with operational efficiency, delivers spaces that stand out in a competitive market.</p><p>The TwentyOne06 Specialty: Elevated, Branded Interiors in the UAE</p><p>Dental Nation is just one example of how TwentyOne06 is redefining healthcare interiors. From dental practices to wellness clinics, our strength lies in creating spaces that feel less like institutions and more like experiences. By fusing brand, hospitality, and functionality, we design environments that patients trust, remember, and return to.</p>',
    false, 2, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    '7bfe5f39-3447-4cb0-a2fb-03b4aa922187', 'twentyone06-shortlisted-across-5-categories-at-cid-awards-2025-mena', 'TwentyOne06 Shortlisted Across 5 Categories at CID Awards 2025: MENA', 'This year’s contenders represent the boldest minds and most visionary spaces shaping the future of regional design, from ground-breaking hotel interiors to inspiring workspaces, from emerging talents rewriting the rules',
    '10 Aug 2025', 'Awards', '/journal/twentyone06-shortlisted-across-5-categories-at-cid-awards-20.png', '["This year’s contenders represent the boldest minds and most visionary spaces shaping the future of regional design, from ground-breaking hotel interiors to inspiring workspaces, from emerging talents rewriting the rules to industry leaders setting new standards.","We’re proud that TwentyOne06 is among these trailblazers, shortlisted across 5 categories at the CID Awards 2025: MENA, recognizing excellence in interior design, innovation, and leadership.","Cheese Board","Interior Design Concept of the Year: Retail","Our experiential rebrand of Cheese Board transforms retail into a curated culinary journey, where storytelling, design, and guest experience intersect.","Dental Nation","Interior Design of the Year: Health & Wellness","Cheese Board’s new flagship on Bluewaters Island is not a grocery store wearing theatrical lights. It’s a stage. Commissioned by Grandiose and reimagined by TwentyOne06, the 1,126 sq ft (104.6 sq m) interior translates cheesemaking into a rebranded architecture, materiality, and choreography - reframing product, pedagogy and retail into a single, sensory performance. Not just a rebrand, it’s a supermarket-born concept transformed into a standalone cultural destination.","The Knowledge Academy","Interior Design of the Year: Office","TwentyOne06, known for its expertise in designing commercial spaces with a hospitality-driven approach, has successfully brought its vision to life with the newly completed The Knowledge Academy training center. In collaboration with fit-out specialists Havelock One, the project seamlessly extends the design aesthetic of The Knowledge Academy’s head office while transforming the space to serve a new purpose: providing a dynamic training environment that fosters both focus and inspiration.","Hanaa Azmi","Unsung Hero of the Year","Hanaa Azmi is a Design Storyteller/Marketing and PR Manager at TwentyOne06, an award-winning interior design studio focused on F&B and hospitality in the UAE. With a background in fashion design, fine arts and narrative crafting, she combines creativity and strategy to enhance the studio’s presence. Hanaa curates the studio’s narratives, visual identity and brand campaigns, develops design research packs, thought leadership articles, and secures media coverage, particularly highlighting collaborations with Michelin-starred chefs. Nominated for the Unsung Hero of the Year award at the Commercial Interior Design Awards - MENA 2024, Hanaa’s expertise in storytelling and marketing in Dubai is crucial to TwentyOne06’s success, in building connections between people and meaningful spaces.","TwentyOne06","Boutique Interior Design Firm of the Year","TwentyOne06, launched in 2018, focuses on hospitality and commercial design, with a portfolio that includes notable projects like Dice Café and Claw BBQ. The firm’s growth from a small team to a thriving agency capable of handling large-scale projects is a testament to its expertise and dedication. With over 30 completed projects, primarily in hospitality and F&B, TwentyOne06 continues to pioneer experiential hospitality design, making it a strong contender in this category."]'::jsonb, '<p>This year’s contenders represent the boldest minds and most visionary spaces shaping the future of regional design, from ground-breaking hotel interiors to inspiring workspaces, from emerging talents rewriting the rules to industry leaders setting new standards.</p><p>We’re proud that TwentyOne06 is among these trailblazers, shortlisted across 5 categories at the CID Awards 2025: MENA, recognizing excellence in interior design, innovation, and leadership.</p><p>Cheese Board</p><p>Interior Design Concept of the Year: Retail</p><p>Our experiential rebrand of Cheese Board transforms retail into a curated culinary journey, where storytelling, design, and guest experience intersect.</p><p>Dental Nation</p><p>Interior Design of the Year: Health &amp; Wellness</p><p>Cheese Board’s new flagship on Bluewaters Island is not a grocery store wearing theatrical lights. It’s a stage. Commissioned by Grandiose and reimagined by TwentyOne06, the 1,126 sq ft (104.6 sq m) interior translates cheesemaking into a rebranded architecture, materiality, and choreography - reframing product, pedagogy and retail into a single, sensory performance. Not just a rebrand, it’s a supermarket-born concept transformed into a standalone cultural destination.</p><p>The Knowledge Academy</p><p>Interior Design of the Year: Office</p><p>TwentyOne06, known for its expertise in designing commercial spaces with a hospitality-driven approach, has successfully brought its vision to life with the newly completed The Knowledge Academy training center. In collaboration with fit-out specialists Havelock One, the project seamlessly extends the design aesthetic of The Knowledge Academy’s head office while transforming the space to serve a new purpose: providing a dynamic training environment that fosters both focus and inspiration.</p><p>Hanaa Azmi</p><p>Unsung Hero of the Year</p><p>Hanaa Azmi is a Design Storyteller/Marketing and PR Manager at TwentyOne06, an award-winning interior design studio focused on F&amp;B and hospitality in the UAE. With a background in fashion design, fine arts and narrative crafting, she combines creativity and strategy to enhance the studio’s presence. Hanaa curates the studio’s narratives, visual identity and brand campaigns, develops design research packs, thought leadership articles, and secures media coverage, particularly highlighting collaborations with Michelin-starred chefs. Nominated for the Unsung Hero of the Year award at the Commercial Interior Design Awards - MENA 2024, Hanaa’s expertise in storytelling and marketing in Dubai is crucial to TwentyOne06’s success, in building connections between people and meaningful spaces.</p><p>TwentyOne06</p><p>Boutique Interior Design Firm of the Year</p><p>TwentyOne06, launched in 2018, focuses on hospitality and commercial design, with a portfolio that includes notable projects like Dice Café and Claw BBQ. The firm’s growth from a small team to a thriving agency capable of handling large-scale projects is a testament to its expertise and dedication. With over 30 completed projects, primarily in hospitality and F&amp;B, TwentyOne06 continues to pioneer experiential hospitality design, making it a strong contender in this category.</p>',
    false, 3, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    'e61a02ec-f2fe-4576-aa4b-80c0c164420f', 'dental-nation-interior-design-twentyone06-transforms-polyclinic-to-premium-care-destination', 'Dental Nation - TwentyOne06 Transforms Polyclinic to Premium Care Destination', 'TwentyOne06 Brings Quiet Luxury to Dental Care with the Transformation of Dental Nation. Healthcare and hospitality rarely meet in the middle. However, TwentyOne06 set out to dismantle that divide with',
    '4 Aug 2025', 'Health & Wellness', '/journal/dental-nation-interior-design-twentyone06-transforms-polycli.jpg', '["TwentyOne06 Brings Quiet Luxury to Dental Care with the Transformation of Dental Nation.","Healthcare and hospitality rarely meet in the middle. However, TwentyOne06 set out to dismantle that divide with the transformation of Acacia Medical Centre into the rebranded, reimagined Dental Nation. With a strategy rooted in emotional design, spatial branding, and operational clarity, the project repositions the standard dental clinic into a serene, elevated wellness destination.","This is not just a renovation. It is a repositioning-from a conventional polyclinic environment into a boutique dental wellness center, purposefully crafted to align with a new brand identity and a premium clientele. By integrating hospitality design principles into the medical landscape, TwentyOne06 has created a groundbreaking space that addresses both psychological and physical well-being","Quiet Luxury: The Guiding Concept","From the start, TwentyOne06 developed a clear design direction centered on the principle of Quiet Luxury -an aesthetic approach that leverages restrained elegance, natural textures, and calming tones to evoke serenity. The palette features soft greys, muted greens, and brand-specific blues, layered thoughtfully with light wood finishes and warm brass accents. The idea was to reduce clinical anxiety and transform the guest experience through subconscious visual cues.","Every surface, color, and lighting choice contributes to a spatial rhythm of calm. The project embodies warmth and refinement, without relying on overt ornamentation. In doing so, it redefines what healthcare interiors can look and feel like.","Reception and First Impressions: Establishing Trust Visually","First impressions matter most in healthcare. At Dental Nation, patients are greeted by a softly textured grey reception desk framed by geometric wood cladding and integrated warm lighting. A curved ceiling profile and logo signage subtly signal quality and care from the very first glance. The reception area embodies the concept of refined calm. Lighting is diffused and directional, guiding patients intuitively through the space while avoiding the harsh fluorescents typical in traditional clinics.","A statement wall, frosted glass, and brass details combine for an understated yet premium welcome experience.","Waiting, But Not Passive: An Experiential Approach","The waiting area at Dental Nation rejects the sterile formality of traditional clinics. Instead, it features layered spaces: an organic seating arrangement, a dedicated children’s area in soft neutrals and greens, and a discrete retail corner showcasing dental wellness products.","Upholstery in brand-specific blue and calming green hues balance visual interest and emotional ease. Backlit artwork, circular recessed lighting, and suspended feature lights add subtle theatrics without overwhelming the senses. Soft beige curtains offer privacy without closing off the room’s openness. The entire zone reflects comfort, not confinement.","Corridors - The Connective Tissue","Often overlooked, Dental Nation’s hallways are treated as key experiential pathways. Warm wood tones, brass-framed doors, and lighting integrated within the handrails elevate what could have been transitional spaces into moments of visual and emotional relief. An arc-shaped interactive light feature with a mirror adds dynamism and playfulness-signaling that this is a place of humanity, not just health. Room numbers are mounted in warm light atop the door frames, removing the sterile coldness that usually marks clinical navigation. At the end of the corridor, a natural focal point grounds the journey and invites a sense of arrival, not departure.","Treatment Rooms","Each dental room was crafted to reduce stress and enhance patient confidence. Soft hues of green, natural oak finishes, and warm integrated lighting set the tone. Artwork, suspended lights, and strategically placed screens create an environment that feels less clinical and more curated. Lighting under counters and above the treatment chairs ensures both functionality for practitioners and psychological ease for patients. The design brings a spa-like feel to dentistry-quieting fears and building trust."]'::jsonb, '<p>TwentyOne06 Brings Quiet Luxury to Dental Care with the Transformation of Dental Nation.</p><p>Healthcare and hospitality rarely meet in the middle. However, TwentyOne06 set out to dismantle that divide with the transformation of Acacia Medical Centre into the rebranded, reimagined Dental Nation. With a strategy rooted in emotional design, spatial branding, and operational clarity, the project repositions the standard dental clinic into a serene, elevated wellness destination.</p><p>This is not just a renovation. It is a repositioning-from a conventional polyclinic environment into a boutique dental wellness center, purposefully crafted to align with a new brand identity and a premium clientele. By integrating hospitality design principles into the medical landscape, TwentyOne06 has created a groundbreaking space that addresses both psychological and physical well-being</p><p>Quiet Luxury: The Guiding Concept</p><p>From the start, TwentyOne06 developed a clear design direction centered on the principle of Quiet Luxury -an aesthetic approach that leverages restrained elegance, natural textures, and calming tones to evoke serenity. The palette features soft greys, muted greens, and brand-specific blues, layered thoughtfully with light wood finishes and warm brass accents. The idea was to reduce clinical anxiety and transform the guest experience through subconscious visual cues.</p><p>Every surface, color, and lighting choice contributes to a spatial rhythm of calm. The project embodies warmth and refinement, without relying on overt ornamentation. In doing so, it redefines what healthcare interiors can look and feel like.</p><p>Reception and First Impressions: Establishing Trust Visually</p><p>First impressions matter most in healthcare. At Dental Nation, patients are greeted by a softly textured grey reception desk framed by geometric wood cladding and integrated warm lighting. A curved ceiling profile and logo signage subtly signal quality and care from the very first glance. The reception area embodies the concept of refined calm. Lighting is diffused and directional, guiding patients intuitively through the space while avoiding the harsh fluorescents typical in traditional clinics.</p><p>A statement wall, frosted glass, and brass details combine for an understated yet premium welcome experience.</p><p>Waiting, But Not Passive: An Experiential Approach</p><p>The waiting area at Dental Nation rejects the sterile formality of traditional clinics. Instead, it features layered spaces: an organic seating arrangement, a dedicated children’s area in soft neutrals and greens, and a discrete retail corner showcasing dental wellness products.</p><p>Upholstery in brand-specific blue and calming green hues balance visual interest and emotional ease. Backlit artwork, circular recessed lighting, and suspended feature lights add subtle theatrics without overwhelming the senses. Soft beige curtains offer privacy without closing off the room’s openness. The entire zone reflects comfort, not confinement.</p><p>Corridors - The Connective Tissue</p><p>Often overlooked, Dental Nation’s hallways are treated as key experiential pathways. Warm wood tones, brass-framed doors, and lighting integrated within the handrails elevate what could have been transitional spaces into moments of visual and emotional relief. An arc-shaped interactive light feature with a mirror adds dynamism and playfulness-signaling that this is a place of humanity, not just health. Room numbers are mounted in warm light atop the door frames, removing the sterile coldness that usually marks clinical navigation. At the end of the corridor, a natural focal point grounds the journey and invites a sense of arrival, not departure.</p><p>Treatment Rooms</p><p>Each dental room was crafted to reduce stress and enhance patient confidence. Soft hues of green, natural oak finishes, and warm integrated lighting set the tone. Artwork, suspended lights, and strategically placed screens create an environment that feels less clinical and more curated. Lighting under counters and above the treatment chairs ensures both functionality for practitioners and psychological ease for patients. The design brings a spa-like feel to dentistry-quieting fears and building trust.</p>',
    false, 4, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    '1b153594-658c-4d14-adde-2ec586555d50', 'twentyone06-emerges-as-regional-leader-at-cid-awards-2025-hospitality-with-four-major-wins', 'TwentyOne06 Emerges as Regional Leader at CID Awards 2025: Hospitality with Four Major Wins', 'Dubai-based interior design studio TwentyOne06 has cemented its status as one of the region’s leading forces in hospitality and F&B design, taking home four key recognitions at the Commercial Interior',
    '20 Jun 2025', 'Awards', '/journal/twentyone06-emerges-as-regional-leader-at-cid-awards-2025-ho.png', '["Dubai-based interior design studio TwentyOne06 has cemented its status as one of the region’s leading forces in hospitality and F&B design , taking home four key recognitions at the Commercial Interior Design Hospitality Awards 2025 - including Winner for Best Use of Materials and Highly Commended Hospitality Design Firm of the Year .","Held at The Ritz-Carlton, JBR in Dubai, the Commercial Interior Design Hospitality Awards spotlight the most influential and innovative interior design projects in the Middle East. With a judging panel made up of global industry leaders and experts, the awards are considered one of the most prestigious events in the regional design calendar.","TwentyOne06 was among the most awarded studios of the night , celebrating wins across multiple categories that reflect its bold, experience-led approach to hospitality interiors.","Award Highlights:","Winner - Best Use of Materials in a Project","Flaky Pastry, The Galleria Al Maryah Island - Abu Dhabi","This 159 sq m croissanterie is the brand’s first venture outside Dubai and serves as a showcase of how food, form, and space can intersect to create a cohesive, multisensory experience. Known for its design-led hospitality work, TwentyOne06 has taken Flaky Pastry’s artisanal ethos and translated it into spatial gestures that reflect the very process of croissant-making.","Highly Commended - Best Bar/Lounge Design","Observatory Lounge, Dubai Marriot Harbor Hotel & Suites, Dubai Marina","Observatory Lounge embraces an organic, flowing aesthetic, creating a connection between space and story. Guests are welcomed by textured neutral walls, washed in warm, inviting hues. Two striking wall etchings, detailed maps of Dubai Marina and Palm Jumeirah, anchor the space in its surroundings, a tribute to the city’s evolving landscape. Overhead, a deep-toned cove ceiling, punctuated by soft spotlights, subtly guides the gaze outward, drawing guests into the breath-taking panoramic views. The neutral palette is intentional, serving as a quiet backdrop that allows the ever-changing cityscape to take center stage.","Highly Commended - Hospitality Design Firm of the Year","TwentyOne06, Dubai","In a region teeming with visionary talent, TwentyOne06 stands apart-not simply as an interior design studio, but as a hospitality experience-maker. Since its founding in 2018 by Creative Director Govind Shepley, TwentyOne06 has grown from a humble apartment-based operation to one of the UAE’s most dynamic and rebellious design studios, with a fast-growing global footprint and a portfolio of award-winning F&B and hospitality concepts.","Highly Commended - Best Restaurant Design: Casual","Flaky Pastry, The Galleria Al Maryah Island - Abu Dhabi","As the UAE’s first dedicated croissanterie, Flaky Pastry represents a growing market of food-first lifestyle concepts. Its expansion into Abu Dhabi reflects consumer demand and a maturing design brief, as interiors are expected to offer brand storytelling, operational functionality, and immersive guest experience. For TwentyOne06, the project represents a wider shift in the regional F&B scene. “This project exemplifies our commitment to designing for a new wave of culinary entrepreneurs,” says Sabiha Yusuf. “People who understand the value of space as more than a backdrop-it’s a vehicle for memory and meaning.”"]'::jsonb, '<p>Dubai-based interior design studio TwentyOne06 has cemented its status as one of the region’s leading forces in hospitality and F&amp;B design , taking home four key recognitions at the Commercial Interior Design Hospitality Awards 2025 - including Winner for Best Use of Materials and Highly Commended Hospitality Design Firm of the Year .</p><p>Held at The Ritz-Carlton, JBR in Dubai, the Commercial Interior Design Hospitality Awards spotlight the most influential and innovative interior design projects in the Middle East. With a judging panel made up of global industry leaders and experts, the awards are considered one of the most prestigious events in the regional design calendar.</p><p>TwentyOne06 was among the most awarded studios of the night , celebrating wins across multiple categories that reflect its bold, experience-led approach to hospitality interiors.</p><p>Award Highlights:</p><p>Winner - Best Use of Materials in a Project</p><p>Flaky Pastry, The Galleria Al Maryah Island - Abu Dhabi</p><p>This 159 sq m croissanterie is the brand’s first venture outside Dubai and serves as a showcase of how food, form, and space can intersect to create a cohesive, multisensory experience. Known for its design-led hospitality work, TwentyOne06 has taken Flaky Pastry’s artisanal ethos and translated it into spatial gestures that reflect the very process of croissant-making.</p><p>Highly Commended - Best Bar/Lounge Design</p><p>Observatory Lounge, Dubai Marriot Harbor Hotel &amp; Suites, Dubai Marina</p><p>Observatory Lounge embraces an organic, flowing aesthetic, creating a connection between space and story. Guests are welcomed by textured neutral walls, washed in warm, inviting hues. Two striking wall etchings, detailed maps of Dubai Marina and Palm Jumeirah, anchor the space in its surroundings, a tribute to the city’s evolving landscape. Overhead, a deep-toned cove ceiling, punctuated by soft spotlights, subtly guides the gaze outward, drawing guests into the breath-taking panoramic views. The neutral palette is intentional, serving as a quiet backdrop that allows the ever-changing cityscape to take center stage.</p><p>Highly Commended - Hospitality Design Firm of the Year</p><p>TwentyOne06, Dubai</p><p>In a region teeming with visionary talent, TwentyOne06 stands apart-not simply as an interior design studio, but as a hospitality experience-maker. Since its founding in 2018 by Creative Director Govind Shepley, TwentyOne06 has grown from a humble apartment-based operation to one of the UAE’s most dynamic and rebellious design studios, with a fast-growing global footprint and a portfolio of award-winning F&amp;B and hospitality concepts.</p><p>Highly Commended - Best Restaurant Design: Casual</p><p>Flaky Pastry, The Galleria Al Maryah Island - Abu Dhabi</p><p>As the UAE’s first dedicated croissanterie, Flaky Pastry represents a growing market of food-first lifestyle concepts. Its expansion into Abu Dhabi reflects consumer demand and a maturing design brief, as interiors are expected to offer brand storytelling, operational functionality, and immersive guest experience. For TwentyOne06, the project represents a wider shift in the regional F&amp;B scene. “This project exemplifies our commitment to designing for a new wave of culinary entrepreneurs,” says Sabiha Yusuf. “People who understand the value of space as more than a backdrop-it’s a vehicle for memory and meaning.”</p>',
    false, 5, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    'b63409c1-0139-4824-afa3-a594734442dc', 'can-you-do-this-quicker-dubai-interior-designers-answer-the-burning-age-old-question', '“Can You Do This Quicker?” - Dubai Interior Designers answer the burning age-old question.', 'As designers, we’re no strangers to this age-old query. It’s a fair question-after all, who doesn’t want to see their design dreams materialize in record time? But let’s take a',
    '9 Jan 2025', 'Insights', '/journal/can-you-do-this-quicker-dubai-interior-designers-answer-the-.png', '["As designers, we''re no strangers to this age-old query. It''s a fair question-after all, who doesn''t want to see their design dreams materialize in record time? But let''s take a moment to peel back the layers and ask the experts why good things take time in the world of #restaurantdesign.","Govind Shepley''s Take Creative Director and Founder of TwentyOne06","Empathizing with this sort of request allows us to work around that and set reasonable expectations concerning the timeline. Wearing multiple hats comes naturally to Govind, our Creative Director and Founder. He''s all about empathizing with clients'' tight deadlines while still keeping an eye on the big picture. Whether it''s understanding the urgency behind a hotel''s launch or deciphering the bottom line for a bustling eatery, Govind''s knack for seeing things from all angles helps us strike that delicate balance between speed and substance. At TwentyOne06, the core of every design project lies a story- a narrative, underpinnings from extensive research required to finalize a design concept. Crafting this narrative isn''t just about picking out paint colors; it''s about tapping into the heartbeat of the brand and translating it into a physical space.","Mike Kobzar''s Spin Lead Branding Designer at TwentyOne06","Designer''s usually find themselves in places having to explain their process, how it needs to take the necessary time alloted to allow for creativity. Educating clients on the nuances of branding is a key part of Mike''s gig. It''s not just about slapping a logo on the wall; it''s about crafting an experience that sings the restaurant''s story from every corner. From delving deep into trend reports to brainstorming concepts that''ll stand the test of time, Mike''s philosophy is all about the 80/20 rule: 80% thinking, 20% designing.","But here''s the kicker: greatness can''t be rushed.","From researching the pulse of the market to weaving together threads of culture and history, our design journey is anything but ordinary. Each decision-from the layout of the space to the texture of the napkins-showcases our commitment to designing an experience, not just a space. And speaking of experience, that''s where the magic truly happens. From the moment guests step through the door to the final flourish of dessert, every sight, sound, and sensation is carefully curated to whisk them away. Of course, this doesn''t mean we can''t stick to deadlines. We pride ourselves on our efficiency and dedication to meeting our clients'' needs. However, clients need to understand that great design takes time. We can only deliver our best work when we''re given the time and space to do so. So while we''re more than capable of meeting deadlines, let''s work together to set realistic expectations. Don''t try to fast-track the process; trust us to deliver excellence at a pace that allows for creativity to flourish. So sit back, relax, and let us work our magic."]'::jsonb, '<p>As designers, we''re no strangers to this age-old query. It''s a fair question-after all, who doesn''t want to see their design dreams materialize in record time? But let''s take a moment to peel back the layers and ask the experts why good things take time in the world of #restaurantdesign.</p><p>Govind Shepley''s Take Creative Director and Founder of TwentyOne06</p><p>Empathizing with this sort of request allows us to work around that and set reasonable expectations concerning the timeline. Wearing multiple hats comes naturally to Govind, our Creative Director and Founder. He''s all about empathizing with clients'' tight deadlines while still keeping an eye on the big picture. Whether it''s understanding the urgency behind a hotel''s launch or deciphering the bottom line for a bustling eatery, Govind''s knack for seeing things from all angles helps us strike that delicate balance between speed and substance. At TwentyOne06, the core of every design project lies a story- a narrative, underpinnings from extensive research required to finalize a design concept. Crafting this narrative isn''t just about picking out paint colors; it''s about tapping into the heartbeat of the brand and translating it into a physical space.</p><p>Mike Kobzar''s Spin Lead Branding Designer at TwentyOne06</p><p>Designer''s usually find themselves in places having to explain their process, how it needs to take the necessary time alloted to allow for creativity. Educating clients on the nuances of branding is a key part of Mike''s gig. It''s not just about slapping a logo on the wall; it''s about crafting an experience that sings the restaurant''s story from every corner. From delving deep into trend reports to brainstorming concepts that''ll stand the test of time, Mike''s philosophy is all about the 80/20 rule: 80% thinking, 20% designing.</p><p>But here''s the kicker: greatness can''t be rushed.</p><p>From researching the pulse of the market to weaving together threads of culture and history, our design journey is anything but ordinary. Each decision-from the layout of the space to the texture of the napkins-showcases our commitment to designing an experience, not just a space. And speaking of experience, that''s where the magic truly happens. From the moment guests step through the door to the final flourish of dessert, every sight, sound, and sensation is carefully curated to whisk them away. Of course, this doesn''t mean we can''t stick to deadlines. We pride ourselves on our efficiency and dedication to meeting our clients'' needs. However, clients need to understand that great design takes time. We can only deliver our best work when we''re given the time and space to do so. So while we''re more than capable of meeting deadlines, let''s work together to set realistic expectations. Don''t try to fast-track the process; trust us to deliver excellence at a pace that allows for creativity to flourish. So sit back, relax, and let us work our magic.</p>',
    false, 6, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    'd037c17c-05e3-4461-ab35-1ca7b5db40ae', 'design-storytelling-press-at-twentyone06-2024-for-far-4', 'Plate to perception - The marketing impact of a restaurant’s interior design.', 'Where every bite competes for attention, restaurants are increasingly recognizing the importance of not only serving delicious cuisine but also providing diners with guest experience they will remember. At the',
    '9 Jan 2025', 'Hospitality', '/journal/design-storytelling-press-at-twentyone06-2024-for-far-4.jpg', '["Where every bite competes for attention, restaurants are increasingly recognizing the importance of not only serving delicious cuisine but also providing diners with guest experience they will remember. At the forefront of this movement is the art of interior design and branding, which shape consumer perceptions and drive marketing success.","But what is it about a thoughtfully arranged space that speaks volumes to diners?","The answer lies in the subtle nuances of psychology. From the placement of tables to the choice of color palette, every aspect of restaurant design is carefully orchestrated to evoke specific emotions and behaviors.","In his best-selling book ''Restaurant Excellence'', Marvin Alballi states, \"Your guests'' journey to your restaurant (and their eyes'' movement during that process plays an important role in their purchasing decisions.\" The Social Media Effect","In the age of Instagram, where every meal is a photo op, a visually striking interior can be the difference between a fleeting glance and a viral sensation. Nowhere is the influence of restaurant design and branding more evident than in the realm of social media. From hashtag-worthy decor to Insta-worthy backdrops, restaurants that prioritize design not only attract foot traffic but also kick-start a digital buzz that is shared across cyberspace, amplifying reach and influence."]'::jsonb, '<p>Where every bite competes for attention, restaurants are increasingly recognizing the importance of not only serving delicious cuisine but also providing diners with guest experience they will remember. At the forefront of this movement is the art of interior design and branding, which shape consumer perceptions and drive marketing success.</p><p>But what is it about a thoughtfully arranged space that speaks volumes to diners?</p><p>The answer lies in the subtle nuances of psychology. From the placement of tables to the choice of color palette, every aspect of restaurant design is carefully orchestrated to evoke specific emotions and behaviors.</p><p>In his best-selling book ''Restaurant Excellence'', Marvin Alballi states, &quot;Your guests'' journey to your restaurant (and their eyes'' movement during that process plays an important role in their purchasing decisions.&quot; The Social Media Effect</p><p>In the age of Instagram, where every meal is a photo op, a visually striking interior can be the difference between a fleeting glance and a viral sensation. Nowhere is the influence of restaurant design and branding more evident than in the realm of social media. From hashtag-worthy decor to Insta-worthy backdrops, restaurants that prioritize design not only attract foot traffic but also kick-start a digital buzz that is shared across cyberspace, amplifying reach and influence.</p>',
    false, 7, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    '7df6dd92-5740-4711-ab06-b79cd3317269', 'design-storytelling-press-at-twentyone06-2024-for-far-3', 'Harnessing the ‘Power of Weird’ in Design Thinking', 'Do more… with more. One of the key drivers behind the ‘Power of Weird’ is the recognition that diversity of thought leads to more robust and ‘out of the box’',
    '9 Jan 2025', 'Insights', '/journal/design-storytelling-press-at-twentyone06-2024-for-far-3.png', '["Do more... with more.","One of the key drivers behind the ''Power of Weird'' is the recognition that diversity of thought leads to more robust and ''out of the box'' solutions. Creatives can tap into a rich reservoir of creativity by encouraging themselves to bring their unique perspectives, experiences, and ideas to the table. This diversity brings about a culture of experimentation, risk-taking, and open-mindedness, essential ingredients for driving creativity in design thinking.","Creativity through constraints.","Paradoxically, embracing the ''Power of Weird'' often involves imposing constraints on the creative process. By setting boundaries and limitations, designers are forced to think outside the box and explore unconventional solutions. This approach encourages resourcefulness, ingenuity, and lateral thinking, pushing teams to find innovative ways to overcome challenges and achieve their objectives.","Case studies in ''Weirdness'' with design.","In the realm of design, from fashion to architecture, several trailblazing designers have embraced the ''Power of Weird'' to push the boundaries of creativity and innovation. Let''s explore some of these unconventional thinkers:","These designers serve as inspiring examples of how embracing the ''Power of Weird'' can lead to groundbreaking innovation and creative expression across various design disciplines. By challenging conventions and thinking outside the box, they continue to push the boundaries of what''s possible, redefining the future of design in the process. In conclusion, the ''Power of Weird'' represents a potent force for innovation and creativity in design thinking. By embracing novelty, diversity, and non-conformity, organizations can unlock new possibilities, challenge the status quo, and create truly transformative solutions. In a world where differentiation is key, harnessing the weird may be the secret sauce that sets your designs apart from the competition."]'::jsonb, '<p>Do more... with more.</p><p>One of the key drivers behind the ''Power of Weird'' is the recognition that diversity of thought leads to more robust and ''out of the box'' solutions. Creatives can tap into a rich reservoir of creativity by encouraging themselves to bring their unique perspectives, experiences, and ideas to the table. This diversity brings about a culture of experimentation, risk-taking, and open-mindedness, essential ingredients for driving creativity in design thinking.</p><p>Creativity through constraints.</p><p>Paradoxically, embracing the ''Power of Weird'' often involves imposing constraints on the creative process. By setting boundaries and limitations, designers are forced to think outside the box and explore unconventional solutions. This approach encourages resourcefulness, ingenuity, and lateral thinking, pushing teams to find innovative ways to overcome challenges and achieve their objectives.</p><p>Case studies in ''Weirdness'' with design.</p><p>In the realm of design, from fashion to architecture, several trailblazing designers have embraced the ''Power of Weird'' to push the boundaries of creativity and innovation. Let''s explore some of these unconventional thinkers:</p><p>These designers serve as inspiring examples of how embracing the ''Power of Weird'' can lead to groundbreaking innovation and creative expression across various design disciplines. By challenging conventions and thinking outside the box, they continue to push the boundaries of what''s possible, redefining the future of design in the process. In conclusion, the ''Power of Weird'' represents a potent force for innovation and creativity in design thinking. By embracing novelty, diversity, and non-conformity, organizations can unlock new possibilities, challenge the status quo, and create truly transformative solutions. In a world where differentiation is key, harnessing the weird may be the secret sauce that sets your designs apart from the competition.</p>',
    false, 8, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    'd45cd829-e0a9-4139-a00e-28f8b54b87f6', 'design-storytelling-press-at-twentyone06-2024-for-far-2', 'How the F&B industry ignites hyper-responsiveness and adaptability in design', 'With F&B experiential design, every detail matters. From the layout of the kitchen to the ambiance of the dining area, every decision shapes the guest experience. Yet, what sets F&B',
    '9 Jan 2025', 'Hospitality', '/journal/design-storytelling-press-at-twentyone06-2024-for-far-2.png', '["With F&B experiential design, every detail matters. From the layout of the kitchen to the ambiance of the dining area, every decision shapes the guest experience. Yet, what sets F&B design apart from other sectors is its fast-paced nature, constantly pushing designers to be hyper-responsive and adaptable.","Why is there a need for speed?","The F&B industry operates at a relentless pace, driven by ever-changing consumer tastes, seasonal ingredients, and evolving trends. Statista states, \"Total revenue is expected to show an annual growth rate (CAGR 2022-2027) of 11.38%, resulting in a projected market volume of US$3.80bn by 2027.\"","Real-time feedback loops.","Unlike other design sectors where projects unfold over months or even years, F&B designers receive immediate feedback from customers, chefs, and operators. This real-time feedback loop enables F&B designers to swiftly iterate and refine their designs to better meet the needs and expectations of their clients. Whether it''s adjusting seating arrangements for better flow or optimizing kitchen layouts for efficiency, F&B designers must be agile in responding to feedback to ensure operations and guest experience.","High levels of service.","Operational optimization in F&B design is intricately linked to the industry''s fast-paced nature, demanding designers to be hyper-responsive and adaptable. In this environment, where efficiency is paramount for high-volume service, designers must create layouts that optimize workflow and facilitate smooth operations, necessitating quick adjustments during peak times. As Marvin Alballi, best-selling author of ''Restaurant Excellence'' aptly states, \"A great restaurant concept without operational excellence equals a total waste of money.\" Moreover, the rapid pace of service requires designers to anticipate and accommodate changing operational needs, necessitating a proactive approach to design that allows for quick modifications without disrupting service. This feedback-driven iteration ensures that the design effectively supports the dynamic demands of restaurant operations, maintaining high levels of service and guest satisfaction.","Thriving on change.","The F&B industry thrives on change, with menus rotating seasonally, culinary trends evolving, and pop-up concepts emerging overnight. Designers must embrace this constant state of flux, designing flexible and adaptable spaces that can easily transition between different F&B concepts. Alballi suggests that designing F&B spaces requires a holistic approach that balances aesthetics with functionality, ensuring that both front-of-house and back-of-house areas are optimized for efficiency and guest satisfaction.","The freedom to experiment.","The fast-paced nature of the F&B industry fosters a culture of innovation and collaboration among designers, chefs, operators, and other stakeholders. Designers have the freedom to experiment with unconventional design concepts, materials, and layouts, pushing the boundaries of creativity to create truly unique and memorable dining experiences. Collaboration between designers and industry professionals ensures that design solutions are not only visually appealing but also operationally sound, reflecting the brand''s ethos and meeting the needs of both guests and operators alike. In conclusion, the fast-paced nature of the F&B industry acts as a catalyst for design innovation, pushing designers to be hyper-responsive, adaptable, and creative in their approach."]'::jsonb, '<p>With F&amp;B experiential design, every detail matters. From the layout of the kitchen to the ambiance of the dining area, every decision shapes the guest experience. Yet, what sets F&amp;B design apart from other sectors is its fast-paced nature, constantly pushing designers to be hyper-responsive and adaptable.</p><p>Why is there a need for speed?</p><p>The F&amp;B industry operates at a relentless pace, driven by ever-changing consumer tastes, seasonal ingredients, and evolving trends. Statista states, &quot;Total revenue is expected to show an annual growth rate (CAGR 2022-2027) of 11.38%, resulting in a projected market volume of US$3.80bn by 2027.&quot;</p><p>Real-time feedback loops.</p><p>Unlike other design sectors where projects unfold over months or even years, F&amp;B designers receive immediate feedback from customers, chefs, and operators. This real-time feedback loop enables F&amp;B designers to swiftly iterate and refine their designs to better meet the needs and expectations of their clients. Whether it''s adjusting seating arrangements for better flow or optimizing kitchen layouts for efficiency, F&amp;B designers must be agile in responding to feedback to ensure operations and guest experience.</p><p>High levels of service.</p><p>Operational optimization in F&amp;B design is intricately linked to the industry''s fast-paced nature, demanding designers to be hyper-responsive and adaptable. In this environment, where efficiency is paramount for high-volume service, designers must create layouts that optimize workflow and facilitate smooth operations, necessitating quick adjustments during peak times. As Marvin Alballi, best-selling author of ''Restaurant Excellence'' aptly states, &quot;A great restaurant concept without operational excellence equals a total waste of money.&quot; Moreover, the rapid pace of service requires designers to anticipate and accommodate changing operational needs, necessitating a proactive approach to design that allows for quick modifications without disrupting service. This feedback-driven iteration ensures that the design effectively supports the dynamic demands of restaurant operations, maintaining high levels of service and guest satisfaction.</p><p>Thriving on change.</p><p>The F&amp;B industry thrives on change, with menus rotating seasonally, culinary trends evolving, and pop-up concepts emerging overnight. Designers must embrace this constant state of flux, designing flexible and adaptable spaces that can easily transition between different F&amp;B concepts. Alballi suggests that designing F&amp;B spaces requires a holistic approach that balances aesthetics with functionality, ensuring that both front-of-house and back-of-house areas are optimized for efficiency and guest satisfaction.</p><p>The freedom to experiment.</p><p>The fast-paced nature of the F&amp;B industry fosters a culture of innovation and collaboration among designers, chefs, operators, and other stakeholders. Designers have the freedom to experiment with unconventional design concepts, materials, and layouts, pushing the boundaries of creativity to create truly unique and memorable dining experiences. Collaboration between designers and industry professionals ensures that design solutions are not only visually appealing but also operationally sound, reflecting the brand''s ethos and meeting the needs of both guests and operators alike. In conclusion, the fast-paced nature of the F&amp;B industry acts as a catalyst for design innovation, pushing designers to be hyper-responsive, adaptable, and creative in their approach.</p>',
    false, 9, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.journal_posts (
    id, slug, title, excerpt, date, tag, image, body, body_html, featured, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    '1bfe64a3-45f3-4104-ab01-d153d9132f92', 'design-storytelling-press-at-twentyone06-2024-for-far', 'Design storytelling/press at TwentyOne06 - 2024 for far', 'Over the past six months, TwentyOne06 has received significant recognition from the industry and the media. We are incredibly proud of our team’s hard work and dedication, which has led',
    '18 Feb 2024', 'Studio News', '/journal/design-storytelling-press-at-twentyone06-2024-for-far.png', '["Over the past six months, TwentyOne06 has received significant recognition from the industry and the media. We are incredibly proud of our team''s hard work and dedication, which has led to numerous press features and award mentions. We want to take a moment to reflect on these accomplishments and share our journey with you.","Why your restaurant’s success hinges on more than the food you serve.","The Story:","At TwentyOne06, we understand that diners seek more than just a meal-they crave memorable moments that engage all senses. From ambient lighting to ergonomic seating and open kitchen concepts, every design element should weave together to tell a compelling story and evoke emotions. By prioritizing comfort, transparency, and efficiency, restaurants can foster intimacy, build trust, and enhance overall guest satisfaction. In Dubai''s dining scene, superior restaurant design isn''t just a luxury, says Govind Shepley, the creative director and founder, it''s a strategic necessity for standing out and capturing diners'' hearts.","Govind Shepley speaks at #INDEXDesignTalks discussing \"Design Alchemy - The Shifting Tides of Interior Design Trends\".","The Story:","Govind Shepley speaks at #INDEXDesignTalks discussing \"Design Alchemy - The Shifting Tides of Interior Design Trends\".","Along with a handful of the industry''s best experts, our Creative Director and Founder Govind Shepley took part in the insightful Executive Think Tank Panel at INDEX discussing \"Design Alchemy - The Shifting Tides of Interior Design Trends\". The panel explored:","Experiential Design: A 10-step approach to elevating F&B spaces.","The Story:","Extracted from our trend reports, Govind Shepley of TwentyOne06 shares their ten-step approach to creating memorable and immersive dining experiences in F&B spaces. This method includes branding, balancing functionality with aesthetics, introducing focal points, guiding the guest experience, incorporating theatrics, and much more. By focusing on these elements, TwentyOne06 ensures that every restaurant they design stands out and resonates deeply with diners.","Behind the design of Reif Othman’s Nama Yoso.","The Story:","A true collaboration with Reif Othman, TwentyOne06 crafted a narrative-driven branding and interior design direction, emphasizing natural elements and Japanese traditions. The restaurant’s color palette-tranquil blue, salmon-inspired orange, and traditional beige-reflects its deep connection to nature. This cohesive storytelling extends to every detail, from the logo to the menu, creating an immersive and authentic dining experience.","The Art of Detailing.","The Story:","Award-winning design firm TwentyOne06 and award-winning fit-out firm Havelock One Interiors have completed a stunning resimercial workspace for The Knowledge Academy in Dubai. This project, blending residential comfort with commercial functionality, exemplifies a hospitality-driven approach to office design. Luxurious materials like marble and brass, combined with warm wood finishes, create an elegant yet practical environment. Thoughtful touches, such as bespoke lighting and plush seating, ensure a workspace that is both opulent and operationally effective. This collaboration sets a new standard for resimercial excellence in Dubai''s business landscape.","TwentyOne06’s journey with Pitfire Pizza Dubai Hills.","The Story:","At TwentyOne06, our collaboration with Pitfire Pizza International exemplifies this approach, where every design element serves as a storytelling medium. From embracing Pitfire’s rebellious spirit and culinary heritage to incorporating anarchitectural elements and celebrating artistic roots, our design aimed to amplify the brand’s ethos. By hero-ing brand-centric materials, colors, and textures, we crafted a space that not only reflects Pitfire’s vibrant personality but also enhances guest engagement and connection.","How older venues can subtly tweak their design to reinvigorate business.","The Story:","Govind Shepley, founder of TwentyOne06, discusses how established F&B venues can strategically refresh their appeal while maintaining their core identity. He emphasizes leveraging materiality and design direction to amplify the venue''s narrative, highlighting culinary techniques and artistic connections. By enhancing existing strengths rather than reinventing them, TwentyOne06 creates immersive guest experiences that resonate with loyal patrons and attract new audiences. The approach involves carefully curated materials to achieve a premium ambiance, fostering community engagement through thoughtful design that sets new standards in Dubai’s competitive dining landscape.","Nama Yoso - Honorable Mention in Interior Design.","The Story:","Nama Yoso has been shortlisted as the winner of the Honourable Mention in Interior Design at the LIV Hospitality Design Awards 2024.","Five designers on balancing luxury with functionality in F&B design, and how they judge venue interiors.","The Story:","Govind Shepley, Creative Director at TwentyOne06, emphasizes practicality as fundamental in F&B design, prioritizing functionality to ensure operational efficiency before layering on opulence. He underscores meticulous attention to detail in finishes and spatial layout to enhance guest experience and operational success. Shepley''s approach integrates luxury seamlessly within functional spaces, aligning with business needs while meeting the region''s expectations for opulent dining environments. His insights from the Hospitality Leadership & F&B Forum at The Hotel Show Dubai highlight a strategic balance in design that caters to both operational efficacy and aesthetic appeal in Dubai''s competitive hospitality market.","Meet the 10 interior designers in the running for CID Awards 2024: Hospitality Designer of the Year.","The Story:","The Creative Director of TwentyOne06 has been shortlisted for the CID Awards 2024: Hospitality Designer of the Year, a prestigious recognition within the MENA region''s hospitality sector. Known for his data-driven precision and innovative approach, Shepley has made a significant impact through collaborations with industry giants like Jumeirah and Marriott. His designs are celebrated for their ability to resonate deeply with users while maintaining a high standard of functionality and aesthetic appeal. Shepley''s nomination reflects his leadership in transforming TwentyOne06 and his influence in shaping contemporary hospitality design in Dubai."]'::jsonb, '<p>Over the past six months, TwentyOne06 has received significant recognition from the industry and the media. We are incredibly proud of our team''s hard work and dedication, which has led to numerous press features and award mentions. We want to take a moment to reflect on these accomplishments and share our journey with you.</p><p>Why your restaurant’s success hinges on more than the food you serve.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>At TwentyOne06, we understand that diners seek more than just a meal-they crave memorable moments that engage all senses. From ambient lighting to ergonomic seating and open kitchen concepts, every design element should weave together to tell a compelling story and evoke emotions. By prioritizing comfort, transparency, and efficiency, restaurants can foster intimacy, build trust, and enhance overall guest satisfaction. In Dubai''s dining scene, superior restaurant design isn''t just a luxury, says Govind Shepley, the creative director and founder, it''s a strategic necessity for standing out and capturing diners'' hearts.</p><p>Govind Shepley speaks at #INDEXDesignTalks discussing &quot;Design Alchemy - The Shifting Tides of Interior Design Trends&quot;.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>Govind Shepley speaks at #INDEXDesignTalks discussing &quot;Design Alchemy - The Shifting Tides of Interior Design Trends&quot;.</p><p>Along with a handful of the industry''s best experts, our Creative Director and Founder Govind Shepley took part in the insightful Executive Think Tank Panel at INDEX discussing &quot;Design Alchemy - The Shifting Tides of Interior Design Trends&quot;. The panel explored:</p><p>Experiential Design: A 10-step approach to elevating F&amp;B spaces.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>Extracted from our trend reports, Govind Shepley of TwentyOne06 shares their ten-step approach to creating memorable and immersive dining experiences in F&amp;B spaces. This method includes branding, balancing functionality with aesthetics, introducing focal points, guiding the guest experience, incorporating theatrics, and much more. By focusing on these elements, TwentyOne06 ensures that every restaurant they design stands out and resonates deeply with diners.</p><p>Behind the design of Reif Othman’s Nama Yoso.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>A true collaboration with Reif Othman, TwentyOne06 crafted a narrative-driven branding and interior design direction, emphasizing natural elements and Japanese traditions. The restaurant’s color palette-tranquil blue, salmon-inspired orange, and traditional beige-reflects its deep connection to nature. This cohesive storytelling extends to every detail, from the logo to the menu, creating an immersive and authentic dining experience.</p><p>The Art of Detailing.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>Award-winning design firm TwentyOne06 and award-winning fit-out firm Havelock One Interiors have completed a stunning resimercial workspace for The Knowledge Academy in Dubai. This project, blending residential comfort with commercial functionality, exemplifies a hospitality-driven approach to office design. Luxurious materials like marble and brass, combined with warm wood finishes, create an elegant yet practical environment. Thoughtful touches, such as bespoke lighting and plush seating, ensure a workspace that is both opulent and operationally effective. This collaboration sets a new standard for resimercial excellence in Dubai''s business landscape.</p><p>TwentyOne06’s journey with Pitfire Pizza Dubai Hills.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>At TwentyOne06, our collaboration with Pitfire Pizza International exemplifies this approach, where every design element serves as a storytelling medium. From embracing Pitfire’s rebellious spirit and culinary heritage to incorporating anarchitectural elements and celebrating artistic roots, our design aimed to amplify the brand’s ethos. By hero-ing brand-centric materials, colors, and textures, we crafted a space that not only reflects Pitfire’s vibrant personality but also enhances guest engagement and connection.</p><p>How older venues can subtly tweak their design to reinvigorate business.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>Govind Shepley, founder of TwentyOne06, discusses how established F&amp;B venues can strategically refresh their appeal while maintaining their core identity. He emphasizes leveraging materiality and design direction to amplify the venue''s narrative, highlighting culinary techniques and artistic connections. By enhancing existing strengths rather than reinventing them, TwentyOne06 creates immersive guest experiences that resonate with loyal patrons and attract new audiences. The approach involves carefully curated materials to achieve a premium ambiance, fostering community engagement through thoughtful design that sets new standards in Dubai’s competitive dining landscape.</p><p>Nama Yoso - Honorable Mention in Interior Design.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>Nama Yoso has been shortlisted as the winner of the Honourable Mention in Interior Design at the LIV Hospitality Design Awards 2024.</p><p>Five designers on balancing luxury with functionality in F&amp;B design, and how they judge venue interiors.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>Govind Shepley, Creative Director at TwentyOne06, emphasizes practicality as fundamental in F&amp;B design, prioritizing functionality to ensure operational efficiency before layering on opulence. He underscores meticulous attention to detail in finishes and spatial layout to enhance guest experience and operational success. Shepley''s approach integrates luxury seamlessly within functional spaces, aligning with business needs while meeting the region''s expectations for opulent dining environments. His insights from the Hospitality Leadership &amp; F&amp;B Forum at The Hotel Show Dubai highlight a strategic balance in design that caters to both operational efficacy and aesthetic appeal in Dubai''s competitive hospitality market.</p><p>Meet the 10 interior designers in the running for CID Awards 2024: Hospitality Designer of the Year.</p><p>The Story:</p><p>The Creative Director of TwentyOne06 has been shortlisted for the CID Awards 2024: Hospitality Designer of the Year, a prestigious recognition within the MENA region''s hospitality sector. Known for his data-driven precision and innovative approach, Shepley has made a significant impact through collaborations with industry giants like Jumeirah and Marriott. His designs are celebrated for their ability to resonate deeply with users while maintaining a high standard of functionality and aesthetic appeal. Shepley''s nomination reflects his leadership in transforming TwentyOne06 and his influence in shaping contemporary hospitality design in Dubai.</p>',
    false, 10, true
  );
INSERT INTO public.testimonials (
    id, quote, name, role, image, status, sort_order, published
  ) VALUES (
    'e8cff699-788b-429f-abb9-f07ea33f0e42', 'The team exceeded our expectations with their exceptional design and development skills. They truly understood our vision and brought it to life. We couldn’t be happier with the final product.', 'Steven Batchelor Frios',
    'Managing Director . UN!Que Project Solutions', '', 'approved', 0, true
